module test.claim.fleet.fleet_host_smbios_observation_witness

// P3 of gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_authority: the fleet lane's in-band SMBIOS producer, witnessed at the
// interface that matters — the standing a reading gets, the source vocabulary it reuses, the evidence it cites,
// and what A2 (gunbc.fleet.fleet_machine_unit_binding) and its real consumer (gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_backing's
// HostBacking.unit, as gunbc.fleet.fleet_enrollment builds it for srv4) do with it.
//
// THE ACCEPTANCE, CLAIM BY CLAIM. srv4's reading is recorded and A2 still admits it — bound at the admission,
// and Resolved at the allocation standing a flip actually reads. Then the other half of the same sentence: a
// refusal stops that machine's cutover. Each refusal case is PLANTED — a reading this producer cannot produce
// from a real host, built here to exercise the shape — and each ends the same way: no observation, so the
// machine never joins A2 and its backing row stays HostUnitUnobserved. The contradiction case plants the BMC FRU
// arm of the SAME observation list A2 folds, which is what reusing gunbc.machine_intake.subject's
// BoardSerialSource buys: an in-band serial that disagrees with the out-of-band one is refused by the binding
// authority, not reconciled here.
//
// Nothing here touches a host. The live read was already taken, read-only, and committed under
// artifacts/host-observations/srv4-inband-smbios-2026-11-11/; the transcript claims below re-read that file.

